WEBVTT

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.620
Allow me to introduce you.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.870
This is Yuki Rurikawa, who will be
helping us with costumes.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.950
Hello.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.660
A girl?

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.500
<i>Excuse </i>me?

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.330
S-Sorry! Maybe not.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.370
You a student?

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.080
Third year of middle school.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.080
I sell my clothing online,
so I don't see an issue.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.450
Don't you have exams if you're a third year--

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.000
I go to an escalator school. Keep your nose out.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.330
He's got a sharp tongue. Like a Masumi #2.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:44.830
Anyway, I hear your show's coming up fast,
so I came for a quick look at you actors.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.370
Energy Concentrate.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.830
Villager C.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.120
Psycho Stalker.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.580
--Foreign Swindler.
--Ooh...

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.330
Elite Swindler.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.830
Right. I'll come again
after I draft some designs.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.250
R-Right.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.370
Bye.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:07.200
Um... and this is?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.040
Ah yes, this is our carpenter, Tetsuro!

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.450
You can count on his skill, since he's
helped us since the original troupe days.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.450
Why doesn't he talk?

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.080
What do you mean?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.000
Aw, Tetsuro, don't say that!

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.410
They're holding a conversation...

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:30.200
So many things are moving forward.
It makes me so excited!

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.910
Sorry, guys, you have a minute?

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.330
We need to talk.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.830
What?!

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.370
"A New Challenge"
Are you serious about quitting?

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.410
"A New Challenge"
Yeah.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.200
"A New Challenge"
Ooh, what bad news.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.870
Ooh, what bad news.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.200
Why quit?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.750
Well--

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.000
It's okay.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.250
I'll tell them.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:37.790
I originally joined to use the money I saved
on rent and food on online games.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.160
Even though I'm not into theater,

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.750
I thought it'd work out
if I played a side character.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:50.540
But turns out that I have loads of lines,
and seeing you all try so hard...

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.250
Feels like I'm the only one who doesn't fit in.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:59.450
It's better if I quit now, so you'll have
more time to find a substitute.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:05.040
Itaru, you really have no interest in theater?

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.950
But you came to morning practices!

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.580
Well...

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:16.290
Truthfully, that's just because
you guys sorta made me want to.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.120
Then why--

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.410
It's not going to work out, though.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.700
No way...

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.620
Just quit if you wanna quit.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.120
Hey, Masumi!

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.950
You should quit if you don't wanna do it.
That old geezer said so, too.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:36.290
Yeah, I think this is the best time.
I'll still support you all after if I quit.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:41.410
Didn't you say that we're all like friends
when we slept over on stage together?!

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.200
I was talking about you guys,
not including myself.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.950
Will you take theater seriously if you
discover it's more interesting than games?

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:54.250
Not sure. Nothing's been
more interesting than games for me.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:57.790
It's true that games are the best entertainment.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.500
Theater is, too!

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:03.290
See the difference in passion
Sakuya and I have for theater?

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:13.700
Itaru. You're still unsure, right?

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.870
Each person's passion for theater is different.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:20.290
You can't compare yourself to others.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:24.580
Anyway, the question is whether or not
<i>you </i>want to continue theater with everyone.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.830
That's the most important thing.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.000
If I stay and I figure I still
don't want to continue,

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.000
won't I cause everyone trouble?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.290
So you still care about
the performance and the troupe.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.580
Well, I mean...

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.790
If that's the case, stay a little bit longer!

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:49.540
And if I want to leave after that?
It'll cause more trouble.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.330
I'll make it work.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.040
Give me some time to think.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:12.080
I can't open up to everyone
and work hard alongside them.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.370
I'm not good at creating deep friendships.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:22.620
So it's impossible for me to put my
whole heart and mind into theater like Sakuya.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:27.040
"You've been defeated by NEONEO_NOOB"

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.330
"You've been defeated by NEONEO_NOOB"
Dammit.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.410
Freakin' griefer.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.450
Thank you!

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.830
Director, let me hold that.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.330
Thanks.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.330
Next is the drugstore, yes?

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.580
Yup.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.330
What's wrong?

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:57.540
It's nothing. Let us continue our errands.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:04.120
Director, you believe that
Itaru will stay, right?

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.250
Yeah...

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:10.160
As do I. But I understand
where Itaru is coming from, too.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.370
Huh?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.790
Citron?

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.660
--Run!
--Huh?

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.330
Wh-What?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.000
What's is it, Citron?

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.750
Citron, what's going on--

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.750
Shh! Quiet.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.540
The pursuers came so far...

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:42.750
Pursuers?!

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:47.790
We'll be fine now. Sorry to scare you.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.660
It's okay.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.950
Maybe I shouldn't pry.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:58.290
The truth is that I didn't come
as an exchange student.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.580
What do you--

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.000
I fled from my country.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.910
You're not joking?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.290
I would not joke.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:11.450
It might be better if
I'm not part of the troupe.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.910
That's not--

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:17.000
That's why I understand
where Itaru is coming from.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.160
I don't want to cause trouble.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.910
I'm sure everyone will
want you to stay despite that.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.540
Including me.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.330
How can you say such kind words to me?

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:33.080
I know the effort you're
putting into delivering your lines.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.330
Your acting keeps improving, too.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.200
Everyone thinks so.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:43.040
They want to be with you and
stand on the same stage as you.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:49.580
Itaru said that Spring Troupe
is like a group of friends.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:56.660
But as for me, I'd be so happy
if we could be like a family.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.830
Wh--? C-Citron?

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.370
<i>Shukran</i>.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.040
What was that?

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.500
Thank you.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.370
I'll follow you, Director.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.290
Citron?!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:24.040
A kiss of loyalty. This is
customary in my country.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:27.160
I-I see...

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.830
Wait!

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.040
Masumi?

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.200
Wait, Dad!

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.040
Wh--?

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.950
Say the divorce isn't true!

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.660
What's wrong with you?

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.500
Pops!

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.200
Dad!

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.950
Mom's crying! You actually
believe in us, don't you?!

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.160
Hang on! I'll get Mom!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.200
Even Tsuzuru and Sakuya?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:05.790
Mom! Look, Dad's leaving!
You've got to stop him!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.950
Huh? Is Director the mom?

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.580
M-My darling!

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:18.950
My darling! I'll play slots with you!

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.660
What the-- It's Citron?!

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:26.700
Please reconsider! Everyone knows you're
an alcoholic and addicted to gambling!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.910
Dude, they made me a terrible character.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.950
--Exacta and trifecta bets...

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.250
--Mom married you knowing all that about you!
--Exacta and trifecta bets...

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.950
--Mom married you knowing all that about you!

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.500
Pops, reconsider!

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.620
Please don't say you're leaving us!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.500
Aren't we a family?

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:02.500
I... want to keep living with you, Dad.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:04.620
Pops!

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:05.620
Dad!

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.330
My darling!

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:20.080
You guys are such idiots.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.750
We put our heads together
to figure out a way to make you stay.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.080
And?

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.500
We'll make you get serious through acting.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.830
So please, stand on the same stage with us!

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:42.700
Please believe in us, Itaru!

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:49.080
Sakuya, you're sounding like a proper lead.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:53.790
Okay. I'll stay until we
finish <i>Romeo and Julius</i>.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.660
--Will you really?
--Yeah.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.160
--Yay! Itaru, thank you!

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.200
--And they lived cabbagely ever after.
--Yay! Itaru, thank you!

00:11:59.200 --> 00:11:59.700
--You mean "lived happily."
--Yay! Itaru, thank you!

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.250
--You mean "lived happily."
--Yeah, yeah. Get off me.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:03.410
--I'm so glad, though.
--I'm so happy! Let's work hard together!
--Yeah, yeah. Get off me.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.870
Just say you're gonna do it.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:12.910
Things are more complicated for adults.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.500
See you, Itaru!

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.540
Don't be late, guys.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.750
Well...

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:31.160
I guess I can try believing in people again.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:40.700
Let's go on a journey together, Julius.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:45.160
We can ditch this cramped town
and travel the world.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:50.540
You've got brawn, Romeo, and I've got brains.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.580
--One day, the town's future
will hinge upon you.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.540
--Good.
--One day, the town's future
will hinge upon you.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.660
--I'm worried about you, Julius.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:57.910
--Everyone's movements look natural.
--I'm worried about you, Julius.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.120
--Everyone's movements look natural.
--O God, have mercy on the innocent.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:01.080
--O God, have mercy on the innocent.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:02.450
All that's left is...

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:14.120
Mm... Not bad.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:19.000
You lot improved a bunch in a short time.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.160
--I'm so relieved. It's all thanks to everyone!

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:21.450
--Man...
--I'm so relieved. It's all thanks to everyone!

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.910
--We shunt him up, huh?
--I'm so relieved. It's all thanks to everyone!

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:29.750
But... the climax ain't exciting enough.
It's missin' somethin'.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:31.870
That 'cause of the script?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.910
If anythin', it's on the direction.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:39.950
How 'bout add a simple sword fight in one of
Romeo and Julius' scenes near the end?

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.040
A sword fight?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.830
We've never had that sort of practice, though.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.290
I'll teach them personally.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:47.540
You mean it?

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:51.410
Yeah! Your enthusiasm's rubbed off on me.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.290
Get ready, 'cause I ain't goin' easy on you!

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:56.410
Thank you so much!

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.870
You're late!

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:05.620
Pound the sequence of movements into your body!

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.700
He's harsh.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.700
Ruthless.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.040
Er, how about a quick break?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.950
Tch. Five-minute breather!

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.580
Sorry.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.750
What'd you think of my sword fighting?

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:31.750
You've got good instincts for this
and your form looks great.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:35.790
My ability's the issue here, huh?

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:40.000
You've been overworking yourself recently.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.950
You're doing this in addition to
our regular rehearsals.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:46.580
You should skip morning practice for now.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.660
I'm fine. I can do it!

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.250
Don't hold us back.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:51.160
Sorry!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.790
Masumi, don't say it like that.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:57.250
Sakuya...

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.160
I'm fine now. We can start again.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.870
While I step back here...

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:24.660
Sakuya...

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.700
Whoa!

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.540
Sakuya!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.200
Are you okay?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.200
Director...

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.870
You're still up practicing?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.000
You've got school tomorrow. Go to sleep!

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.040
Just a little more--

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.370
Nope! That's a direct order!

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.450
There's no point if you
injure yourself overdoing it!

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.870
Okay...

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:50.950
No need to attend morning rehearsal.
Get some rest.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.870
Good night.

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.830
Sorry I'm late!

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.870
Sakuya, I said you didn't need to come.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.410
You need to get proper rest!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:17.250
Sorry. I'm fine, though.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.370
Whoa, Sakuya. You all right?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.540
I'm fine.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.950
Bobbly on your feet.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.040
You mean "wobbly."

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.620
Listen up, guys.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:34.580
We're cutting the sword fight from the play.

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:37.370
Yeah, that's a good idea.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:39.660
Why?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:44.120
We're putting too much on Sakuya.
It'll all be for nothing

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.620
if he injures himself or collapses
before the performance.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.410
I'm fine. I can still keep going!

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:53.830
I agree with the director.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:56.580
You shouldn't overdo it.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.040
I can do it.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:02.700
There's no point in the sword fight
if you don't do it together.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:08.080
Then just switch out Romeo.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.000
What are you talking--

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.250
The sword fight will be better that way.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:15.950
Masumi, that's not how it works!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:19.750
The old geezer said that it
wasn't exciting enough anyway.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:20.830
No way.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:23.160
No way! I'm never giving it up!

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.410
Romeo is <i>my </i>role!

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:28.000
C-C'mon Sakuya. Chill out.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:32.910
I'm never giving up my role as Romeo!

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:34.580
--We won't make you.
--Masumi, you're too demanding.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:37.660
--Remember I wrote the role for you?
--Masumi, you're too demanding.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:41.580
Let me continue. I'll do my best.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.250
So, please!

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.250
Fine.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.580
Let's give the sword fight a little more time.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:51.950
However, no overdoing it in practice.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.540
It's also an actor's job
to care for their bodies.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:57.080
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.000
Sakuya.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.200
It's so late. What's up?

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.500
Director... I couldn't sleep for some reason.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.250
I see.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:24.330
Things don't go right for me
even when I try my best. I always fail.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.660
I got scared thinking things
wouldn't go right again this time.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:33.500
You're getting better.
We're just short on rehearsal time--

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:34.540
It's not that.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.540
Huh?

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.040
It's something else.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:43.830
You know how I've always lived with relatives?

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.080
In the beginning, I always try hard
so that this time around,

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:54.540
I'll get along with them and
open up to them like real family.

00:18:54.540 --> 00:19:00.580
But it never works out, and I end up
going to a different relative.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:06.830
I fail at everything I do.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.290
That's not true.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.000
Relationships depend on you
<i>and </i>the other person.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.620
You don't need to take all the blame.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.540
Thank you.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:26.580
When I finally found a place to belong here
in getting the Romeo role, I was thrilled.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:30.250
It made me feel acknowledged as a troupe member,

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:34.700
so I was scared to lose the Romeo role.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:36.500
That's why.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:40.040
How did you first come to like theater?

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:43.500
I first got interested watching
a play in elementary school.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:49.450
The actors were all so lively
and seemed like real pirates.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:52.250
I was mesmerized.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:57.290
During the play, the fire alarm went off.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:03.700
Scallywags! We're under navy attack!

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:06.040
Retreat smartly, me mateys!

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.620
Ye know the drill!

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:20.290
I still remember those lines today.

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:22.700
The students, who were close to panic,

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.500
began evacuating under the captain's orders.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:28.950
It was so exciting!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.870
It felt like I was part of the pirate crew.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:40.160
Even when the actors stepped off stage,
the story continued.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:44.660
The show must go on. The show won't end.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:46.200
Yes!

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:50.950
The show won't end no matter what.
It has to keep going.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:57.160
I wanted a place to belong,
a role just for me that I could take pride in,

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.870
like those actors I saw back then.

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:02.410
I see.

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:07.540
Don't worry, you're the only one
who can pull of this Romeo for us!

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.580
Everybody recognizes that.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:14.080
And Itaru probably stayed thanks to you.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.700
With everyone else's help.

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:22.660
It's the result of all the hard work you've done
for the sake of the troupe as the lead.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.950
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.660
Do you feel better about the sword fight now?

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:32.120
Sorry, but I still want to do it.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.950
You're pretty stubborn.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:38.750
Okay. You can continue if you're
careful not to hurt yourself.

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:42.750
Thank you! Please let me try again tomorrow!

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:47.000
The walls have ears, the doors have Iris,
and behind you is Citron.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.370
Too many people there.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.540
In my country, you'd be punished
to say a tongue twister

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.870
three hundred times fast for eavesdropping.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.410
You're guilty, too.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.660
Ooh, we're accomplices.

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:03.950
I didn't know anything about him.

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:09.830
We'll continue to learn much more...

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:11.660
...about each other.
